\section{What an estimating function returned}{

\itemize{
\item \code{deli_psi_return_error}: the estimating function returned something no
sandwich can be built from, either at the starting values or at the point
handed to \code{\link[=compute_sandwich]{compute_sandwich()}}. Every refusal of a return carries it, so
recognizing one is a match on this rather than on four messages.
\item \code{deli_psi_shape_error}: the number of estimating equations returned cannot
be solved against the number of parameters. Leads \code{deli_psi_return_error}.
\item \code{deli_psi_list_unsupported}: the estimating function returned a list of one
element per equation. \code{\link[=compute_bread]{compute_bread()}} and \code{\link[=compute_sandwich]{compute_sandwich()}} take that
